# Talos gestiona Kubernetes
hetzner.talos_cp -> hetzner.ns_flux.fluxcd: "Kubernetes API\n(talosctl gestiona el OS)"

# =============================================================
# NOTAS
# =============================================================

note_talos: |md
  **Talos Linux v1.10.x — OS Inmutable:**
  - 12 binarios en PATH (Ubuntu: miles)
  - Zero SSH en producción
  - SquashFS firmado y versionado
  - Todo via `talosctl` API + mTLS
  - Upgrade atómico: OS + K8s juntos

  **Single-node, add workers sin downtime:**
  ```
  talosctl gen config worker
  talosctl apply-config --nodes <NEW_IP>
  ```
  → Cluster escala automáticamente
| {
  near: hetzner.talos_cp
  shape: page
  style.fill: "#FFFDE7"
  style.stroke: "#F9A825"
}

note_pg: |md
  **CloudNativePG v1.x:**
  Cluster CRD gestiona:
  - 6 databases en 1 instancia PG
  - WAL archiving continuo → B2
  - PITR a cualquier punto
  - Auto-generated k8s Secrets
    con connection strings para Go

  Extensiones PG:
  pg\_uuidv7 · btree\_gist · hstore

  **Fase 4+:** separar clinical\_db
  en Cluster CRD propio para
  compliance crítico.
| {
  near: hetzner.ns_data.pg
  shape: page
  style.fill: "#FFFDE7"
  style.stroke: "#F9A825"
}

note_traefik: |md
  **Traefik v3.x — Equivalencias vs Caddy:**

  Caddy `forward_auth`
  → Traefik `ForwardAuth Middleware`

  Caddy `reverse_proxy`
  → Traefik `IngressRoute + Service`

  Caddy `TLS automático`
  → cert-manager `ClusterIssuer`

  La lógica IAM (/internal/validate-token)
  NO cambia — solo el llamador cambia
  (Caddy → Traefik ForwardAuth).
| {
  near: hetzner.ns_traefik.traefik
  shape: page
  style.fill: "#FFFDE7"
  style.stroke: "#F9A825"
}

note_fluxcd: |md
  **GitOps con FluxCD v2.x:**
  Git es la ÚNICA fuente de verdad.
  Ningún `kubectl apply` manual en prod.

  ```
  infra/clusters/hetzner-prod/
  ├── flux-system/    (bootstrap)
  ├── infrastructure/ (cert-mgr, traefik, cnpg)
  ├── apps/           (iam, sched, clinical, billing)
  └── secrets/        (SealedSecrets — safe for Git)
  ```

  FluxCD reconcilia cada 1 minuto.
  Drift de config: auto-revertido.
| {
  near: hetzner.ns_flux.fluxcd
  shape: page
  style.fill: "#FFFDE7"
  style.stroke: "#F9A825"
}

note_nats: |md
  **NATS JetStream v2.11.x**
  BREAKING vs v2.10.x.

  4 Streams (NACK CRDs):
  - SERENAMENTE\_IAM:      365d
  - SERENAMENTE\_SCHED:    730d
  - SERENAMENTE\_CLINICAL: sin límite
  - SERENAMENTE\_BILLING:  3650d

  storage=file → PVC (persiste en disco).
  Consumer: explicit ACK.
  MaxDeliver: 5 (retry + DLQ).
| {
  near: hetzner.ns_data.nats
  shape: page
  style.fill: "#FFFDE7"
  style.stroke: "#F9A825"
}

order_note: |md
  **ORDEN DE IMPLEMENTACIÓN — Topología Kubernetes**
  Ref: plans/06_talos_k8s_decision_y_cambios_en_cadena.md

  **FASE 1** — Talos + k8s + IAM + Gateway (~$7.50/mes)
  1.A  Hetzner CX32 + Talos Linux v1.10.x bootstrap
       Kubernetes 1.33.x single-node + FluxCD bootstrap
  1.B  cert-manager + Traefik v3.x + Sealed Secrets
  1.C  CloudNativePG operator + Cluster CRD
       (6 databases, WAL → B2, PITR)
  1.D  Protobuf schemas + buf.build CLI
  1.E  Ory Kratos v1.3.1 (Helm: ory/kratos)
  1.F  IAM Domain Service (Deployment + Service)
       JWT Ed25519 + Outbox Worker + ForwardAuth
  1.G  Cloudflare Workers + Hono v4.x BFF
  1.H  Qwik v2.0 SPA en CF Pages
  1.I  CloudNativePG ScheduledBackup CRD → B2

  **FASE 2** — Motor Médico (~$16/mes)
  2.A  NATS JetStream (Helm: nats/nats, NACK CRDs)
  2.B  Outbox Worker (librería Go compartida)
  2.C  Scheduling Service (Deployment + Service)
  2.D  Clinical Record Service (Deployment + Service)
  2.E  Astro v6.x Landing Page en CF Pages

  **FASE 3** — Plataforma Completa (~$22-27/mes)
  3.A  OpenFGA v1.x (Helm: openfga/openfga)
  3.B  Billing & Ops Service (Deployment + Service)
  3.C  kube-prometheus-stack v82.x + Loki + Tempo
  3.D  Alertmanager → Telegram bot

  **FASE 4+** — Multi-nodo
  talosctl apply-config --nodes <NEW\_CX32>
  → Worker se une sin downtime
| {
  shape: page
  style.fill: "#E8F5E9"
  style.stroke: "#2E7D32"
}
